    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup optimized to exploit favorable matchups against high-xERA starters. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) and **Kyle Tucker** (74.44) anchor our attack, both benefiting from ideal platoon splits and high-leverage spots in the batting order against Holmes and Gasser, respectively. **Andy Pages** (69.18) also grades out as an elite play; his matchup against Gasser\u2019s 5.63 xERA represents the highest upside for power production in today\u2019s lineup. We are leaning heavily into **Sam Antonacci** (63.14) at the keystone, as the combination of a favorable wind direction and Houser\u2019s mediocre efficiency makes him a high-floor play, particularly given his leadoff spot.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility spot was tight, with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.94) edging out **Nolan Schanuel** (44.77). While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces an elite arm in Skenes\u2014resulting in a significant 19% downward adjustment for SP skill\u2014his superior raw power metrics kept him ahead of **Nolan Schanuel**, who was benched due to a difficult matchup against Eovaldi. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the status of **Josh Jung** and **Jackson Merrill**, both of whom are currently tagged with \"Lineup Pending\" status; if **Josh Jung** is shifted down from the #2 spot or **Jackson Merrill** is moved out of the order, we will have to pivot quickly. We continue to hold **Gunnar Henderson** on the bench following his confirmed rainout, while **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** remain sidelined on the IL, limiting our depth as we navigate this stretch of the season.",
